{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems","id":1342010,"title":"The Worst Lunar Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-17T21:30:15-07:00","id":1342010,"title":"The Worst Lunar Totems","content":"Hey all, I had this thought while browsing Wikipedia when I couldn\u2019t sleep. What would be the worst lunar animal totems? Think of animals that are impractical, gross, or in such an evolutionary niche that they cannot be played (nor would any sane person wish to play them).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll start us off with these little guy/gals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Sacculina_carcini.jpg/1280px-Sacculina_carcini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\"> Rhizocephala - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T00:27:00-07:00","id":1342030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems#post1342010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all, I had this thought while browsing Wikipedia when I couldn\u2019t sleep. What would be the worst lunar animal totems? Think of animals that are impractical, gross, or in such an evolutionary niche that they cannot be played (nor would any sane person wish to play them).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll start us off with these little guy/gals.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you proposing that the Lunar would assume a form that could only parasitize crabs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T00:32:41-07:00","id":1342033,"title":"","content":"how about a Sponge or coral Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T03:07:40-07:00","id":1342047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342033#post1342033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how about a Sponge or coral Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the Lunar Stamina tree, this might actually be pretty scary. An angry Lunar might literally <i>suck up</i> a storm mother\u2019s supernatural weather or a sorcerer\u2019s Mists of Eventide and spit it back out at her, all without ever moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T05:32:17-07:00","id":1342058,"title":"","content":"How 'bout a kiwi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:19:58-07:00","id":1342065,"title":"","content":"Snake. Turning into a snake never helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:30:21-07:00","id":1342072,"title":"","content":"Turning into a snake is super useful.<br /> <br /> No, the worst totem is the one that's fully adapted to something that you're very unlikely to require skill in; eating bamboo.<br /> That being the panda.<br /> What Totemic charms does Panda even let you access?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T07:40:16-07:00","id":1342074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342065#post1342065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snake. Turning into a snake never helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always been a bunk entry on the Evil Overlord List, because when Thulsa Doom did it, he evaded Conan by slithering through a secret passage in the wall, and Jafar was doing pretty well when Scaled Up; had the protagonists on the ropes, in fact. Then he wished to become a genie...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T08:52:01-07:00","id":1342088,"title":"","content":"Ocalot. They're sick all the time.<br /> <br /> (Master cylinder.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:36:46-07:00","id":1342104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342074#post1342074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's always been a bunk entry on the Evil Overlord List, because when Thulsa Doom did it, he evaded Conan by slithering through a secret passage in the wall, and Jafar was doing pretty well when Scaled Up; had the protagonists on the ropes, in fact. Then he wished to become a genie...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It kind of shows the List is a product of a certain period, the 70s, before either of those films. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:54:14-07:00","id":1342110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342104#post1342104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of shows the List is a product of a certain period, the 70s, before either of those films. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify for those who aren't aware, this is a joke; the Evil Overlord List is a product of the early '90s, not the 70s. (Sorry to be pedantic, but it <i>is</i> my earliest source of geek cred. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:03:31-07:00","id":1342111,"title":"","content":"Well, the two Lunars in my group--I have a group again!--are a butterfly-winged tyrant lizard and... a horse. Not saying those are bad, but that is the experience I'm working with.<br /> <br /> As far as worst... maybe the Dung Beetle? Or maybe Japanese freshwater eel? I don't think there are many totemic options for 'goes well on sushi or barbecued'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:59:24-07:00","id":1342127,"title":"","content":"Dung beetles could be master crafters though, plus they\u2019re hardy, very pretty, and have associations with various Egyptian gods.<br /> <br /> Going back to marine life, I think a Tritonia would be a pretty miserable Lunar totem, or any shell-less Gastropoda.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, what would make the Rhizocehyla a bad lunar totem is that it is such an ultra-specialized parasite that it truncates usual life-cycles and doesn\u2019t even really eat, it just destroys its host and reproduces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","user":"Sticks","date":". 10-18-2019, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T11:13:40-07:00","id":1342132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342127#post1342127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to marine life, I think a Tritonia would be a pretty miserable Lunar totem</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they one of those sea slugs that eats animals with poisonous spines that they can then take for themselves?<br /> <br /> Also being really flamboyantly coloured in a manner that causes confusion in predators?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be clear, what would make the Rhizocehyla a bad lunar totem is that it is such an ultra-specialized parasite that it truncates usual life-cycles and doesn\u2019t even really eat, it just destroys its host and reproduces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give such a Lunar licence to do that to enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T11:22:21-07:00","id":1342134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342111#post1342111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as worst... maybe the Dung Beetle? Or maybe Japanese freshwater eel? I don't think there are many totemic options for 'goes well on sushi or barbecued'...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dung beetles go well on sushi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:23:47-07:00","id":1342216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342134#post1342134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dung beetles go well on sushi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or barbecued?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T19:43:43-07:00","id":1342256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342216#post1342216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or barbecued?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the American south Giant June Bugs (same family as Dubg Beetles, scarabaie) are sometimes saut\u00e9ed and served as a side, with the recipe coming from west-African traditions...so I guess they\u2019re good *with* Barbeque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:47:47-07:00","id":1342298,"title":"","content":"What about a maggot? I mean I could see them being respected or feared in a culture as a sign of decay, death, and rot. Still would be a problem to find out your spirit totem is a larval state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:53:27-07:00","id":1342299,"title":"","content":"My play group has had at various points:<br /> A hummingbird Lunar (Played as constantly over-caffeinated)<br /> A Fainting Goat Lunar<br /> and a Human Lunar (character started off as an ata-pard who exalted with a human totem and was annoyed at how useless human limbs are for anything except fine manipulation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:56:52-07:00","id":1342301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342298#post1342298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a maggot? I mean I could see them being respected or feared in a culture as a sign of decay, death, and rot. Still would be a problem to find out your spirit totem is a larval state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your spirit shape grows old right? So in a thousand years you'll be a fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T01:08:56-07:00","id":1342306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342111#post1342111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the two Lunars in my group--I have a group again!--are a butterfly-winged tyrant lizard and... a horse. Not saying those are bad, but that is the experience I'm working with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Turning into a flying Tyrant Lizard or taking centaur on your HBR? (Not to mention the enormous speed bonus.) Those are some power totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T03:38:04-07:00","id":1342319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342299#post1342299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how useless human limbs are for anything except fine manipulation).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which other animal can lift things over its head again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T10:58:42-07:00","id":1342374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342306#post1342306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning into a flying Tyrant Lizard or taking centaur on your HBR? (Not to mention the enormous speed bonus.) Those are some power totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keying your horse totem up as a centaur may lead to adoption of archery, terrible archery accidents firing an arrow out of reflex, and being voiced by Sugita Tomokazu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T11:01:49-07:00","id":1342375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342319#post1342319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which other animal can lift things over its head again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apes, crustaceans, some insects, but I see your point.<br /> <br /> Putting yourself in a larval stage hadn\u2019t occurred to me. There are some pretty neat caterpillars that would make fun totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T11:38:07-07:00","id":1342384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342374#post1342374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keying your horse totem up as a centaur may lead to adoption of archery, terrible archery accidents firing an arrow out of reflex, and being voiced by Sugita Tomokazu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget having a sweet direlance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T12:07:39-07:00","id":1342387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342298#post1342298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a maggot? I mean I could see them being respected or feared in a culture as a sign of decay, death, and rot. Still would be a problem to find out your spirit totem is a larval state.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would make more sense for a library shape, i guess. As you said yourself, a maggot is simply the larval stage of a fly, it ain't a creature on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T12:22:18-07:00","id":1342389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Don't forget having a sweet direlance.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Well, that or a backup diamond tree wooden sword...</span><br /> </span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <hr /></span></span></div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342387#post1342387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would make more sense for a library shape, i guess. As you said yourself, a maggot is simply the larval stage of a fly, it ain't a creature on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've often wondered if that would be something that might crop up with child characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T13:51:23-07:00","id":1342399,"title":"","content":"Or teens.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be quite cool to, say, be a Casteless caterpillar-totem Lunar (focus on camouflage and poison) and then at some point (when you are bored of that) transition to a glorious butterfly-totem Changing Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:39:17-07:00","id":1342432,"title":"","content":"I think metamorphosis is unusual enough as a biological mechanism that it could get some of its own rules as regards spirit shapes. My gut says that larvae are distinct mythologically, and thus valid as totems irrespective of age (nor is metamorphosis a necessity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:10:30-07:00","id":1342505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342432#post1342432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think metamorphosis is unusual enough as a biological mechanism that it could get some of its own rules as regards spirit shapes. My gut says that larvae are distinct mythologically, and thus valid as totems irrespective of age (nor is metamorphosis a necessity).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Must admit i'm of two minds on the subject too - while from a biological standdpoint it's kind of separating age stages, it's also that Creation does not quite follow linnean standards of organization and metamorphosis &amp; change have has certain folkloric/mythic milleage for certain. That said, could it not be covered as species-only &quot;animal power&quot;, like, i don't know the mythic asssociation of snakes with eternal youth/renewwal due to the periodic shedding of skins, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T04:09:10-07:00","id":1342686,"title":"","content":"First off, clearly the people saying &quot;Dung beetle&quot; have never played Hollow Knight.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://tr.rbxcdn.com/fa8be89fcbea85a8d6e7c2ad27f64939/420/420/Decal/Png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously, <i>this guy</i>. Rolls around like crazy and throws boulders of dung at you as an attack.<br /> <br /> And while I'm serious - no totem is going to be absolutely terrible, since you can choose how it might manifest in HBT. Any winged insect will at least be valid for wings, that parasite-crab-thing is still valid for carapace, and so on. You might not use your spirit shape as often as other Lunars, that's all.<br /> <br /> Some totems are definitely not very charismatic or stylish, though. Like... <i>any nematode</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T07:31:51-07:00","id":1342710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342134#post1342134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dung beetles go well on sushi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I guess I had a run-on sentence. I was saying Dung Beetle seemed pretty bad (one thought), and that <i>unagi</i> in terms of usefulness as a totem seemed pretty limited to 'good on sushi'. (Sure, it can presumably work well underwater, but there are other better ones.)<br /> <br /> TheWizardOfOz: Oh, I definitely agree. I was trying to point out that the Lunars I'm playing with don't have anything close to 'bad' totems, and so my experience with this was limited, and thus to take my ideas later (dung beetle and <i>unagi</i>) with a grain of salt. Or pepper, if you prefer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:18:08-07:00","id":1342721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342072#post1342072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the worst totem is the one that's fully adapted to something that you're very unlikely to require skill in; eating bamboo.<br /> That being the panda.<br /> What Totemic charms does Panda even let you access?</div> </div> </div> </div>Panda does seem to fall solidly into the category of animals that seem like they are actively trying to go extinct, but I think Koalas have them beat. Koalas have super specific diets, it's so low in nutrients that the koala has little choice but to be either eating or sleeping and it grinds their teeth down to the point that they eventually starve to death. The only thing Koalas seem to be good at is getting chlamydia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:47:06-07:00","id":1342732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342686#post1342686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, clearly the people saying &quot;Dung beetle&quot; have never played Hollow Knight.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://tr.rbxcdn.com/fa8be89fcbea85a8d6e7c2ad27f64939/420/420/Decal/Png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously, <i>this guy</i>. Rolls around like crazy and throws boulders of dung at you as an attack.<br /> <br /> And while I'm serious - no totem is going to be absolutely terrible, since you can choose how it might manifest in HBT. Any winged insect will at least be valid for wings, that parasite-crab-thing is still valid for carapace, and so on. You might not use your spirit shape as often as other Lunars, that's all.<br /> <br /> Some totems are definitely not very charismatic or stylish, though. Like... <i>any nematode</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nematodes are also too tiny to be totems, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:20:25-07:00","id":1342759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342072#post1342072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the worst totem is the one that's fully adapted to something that you're very unlikely to require skill in; eating bamboo.<br /> That being the panda.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, pandas are barely adapted to eating bamboo. They still have a carnivorous digestive tract, and can only just about digest cellulose via gut flora that they populate themselves with by eating their mother's faeces. They barely derive calories from it, hence why they're a fairly lethargic animal.<br /> <br /> Apparently, they eat bamboo because a random mutation shut off the taste receptors for meat, and they just happened to be around abundant plants that would have been the only thing flavourful to them.<br /> <br /> So they barely adapted enough to have not starved to death, and otherwise coasted by on lack of natural predators.<br /> <br /> Nature is full of mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:24:30-07:00","id":1342793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1342010-the-worst-lunar-totems?p=1342759#post1342759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is, pandas are barely adapted to eating bamboo. They still have a carnivorous digestive tract, and can only just about digest cellulose via gut flora that they populate themselves with by eating their mother's faeces. They barely derive calories from it, hence why they're a fairly lethargic animal.<br /> <br /> Apparently, they eat bamboo because a random mutation shut off the taste receptors for meat, and they just happened to be around abundant plants that would have been the only thing flavourful to them.<br /> <br /> So they barely adapted enough to have not starved to death, and otherwise coasted by on lack of natural predators.<br /> <br /> Nature is full of mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The background mutation rate is a hell of a drug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}